# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (Vite)
#  Copy this file as .env and fill in values as needed.
#  None of these are required for the app to run — every existing
#  feature resolves its own API URL at runtime (see BASE in src/asad.jsx).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Where the frontend's chat socket connects for real-time messaging.
#
# Leave unset for local dev (falls back to http://localhost:5001) or for
# a deployment where the same always-on host serves both the REST API and
# Socket.IO (falls back to the current page's origin).
#
# Set this explicitly if your real-time chat server lives somewhere other
# than your main API host — e.g. your REST API is on Vercel (which can't
# host Socket.IO — see backend/.env.example for why) but you've deployed
# backend/server.js to Render/Railway/Fly.io/a VPS specifically to serve
# chat's WebSocket connections:
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://your-chat-server.onrender.com
